All the facts are gathered. Key observations for the plan:

1. The permitted file scope for FSM-001 is `scripts/fishing/**` and `tests/**`. Notably, `scripts/core/fishing_system.gd` (an existing skeleton with `class_name FishingSystem`) is not included in the permitted scope. This is a critical deviation: the FishingSystem stub lives in scripts/core, but Phase B can only write to scripts/fishing/** and tests/**. So the implementation must be placed under `scripts/fishing/` as new files, and the stub in core must not be touched. A class_name collision must be avoided: the existing skeleton already declares `class_name FishingSystem` in scripts/core/fishing_system.gd. So the new class must use a different class_name. For example `FishingFsm` or `FishingStateMachine` inside `scripts/fishing/`. This is exactly the same as the D-2 deviation in CFG-001 (the ConfigLoader stub occupied that name). We need to document the deviation: implement a new class under scripts/fishing/ with a different name (e.g. `class_name FishingFSM`), or better, don't use a class_name that collides at all.

Wait — but the stub comment in scripts/core/fishing_system.gd says "FSM-001 implementation: state transitions, RNG injection + independent virtual clock, cast wait 20–60 s (in seconds, not frames)", suggesting FSM-001 should implement it there. But the permitted scope forbids touching scripts/core/**. This is a contradiction similar to the D-2 in the CFG-001 plan, and the CFG-001 plan was resolved by putting a new class in an in-scope directory and not touching the out-of-scope stub. Do the same: create `scripts/fishing/fishing_fsm.gd` etc. with a non-colliding class_name (`FishingSystemFSM`? No: `FishingFSM`... hmm `FishingSystem` is taken. Use `class_name FishingStateMachine`). And document deviation D-1.

Alternative: could the FSM be implemented without class_name, with the test preloading by path? That would completely avoid the collision. But a global class_name is more convenient for later ECO-001. Godot's class_name duplication is a compile error. `FishingSystem` is taken by the core stub, so use a different name. Note: can the test preload `res://scripts/fishing/fishing_fsm.gd` regardless of class_name presence? Preloading a script with a class_name is fine. Simplest: use `class_name FishingStateMachine`.

2. RNG and Clock injection: implement a deterministic RNG. Godot has RandomNumberGenerator with seed — deterministic across versions? For test reproducibility, better to implement a small deterministic PRNG inside GDScript (e.g. SplitMix64 / xorshift64*). Deterministic across engines/platforms, and the test asserts that the same seed → same sequence. The INTERFACES pseudo-contract: initialize(config, injected_rng, injected_clock, recovered_checkpoint), can_cast, tick_effective(seconds), request_cast, produce_catch_candidate, ack_settlement, pause/resume_if_safe, snapshot_checkpoint. Implement interfaces close to the doc's semantics: the exact signatures can be recorded, but semantics/invariants are not to be changed.

3. What to cover in tests: T-FSM-01 (reject invalid transitions + full legitimate ordering), T-TIME-01 (wait time within configured [min,max] range; same seed/clock/config reproducible event-by-event), T-TIME-02 (30/15/120 FPS simulation render conditions don't alter the event timeline — i.e., tick with different sub-step sizes summing to the same virtual time and the same events occur; frame counts don't affect timing). Additionally "no settlement completion → no next cast (no cast before settlement completes)", "no extra transactions generated while paused" (T-TIME-03 partial — pause does not generate extra events). Also the ConfigGate gate: reject FSM startup when config is invalid (the FSM must check ConfigGate before start) — good to include: FSM start requires the ConfigGate.can_start_economy gate.

4. Test command pattern: follow the CFG-001 pattern — a Python runner `tests/unit/run_fsm001_checks.py` (stdlib only) that: step1 import (`--editor --quit`), step2 FSM test script, step3 CORE-001 smoke regression, step4 CFG-001 config regression. And/or a direct Godot headless command. test_cmd is empty in the queue; the scheduler will refill (backfill) test_cmd from the plan; per CFG-001 precedent, the queue brief demanded a python runner for CFG-001, but the FSM-001 brief is simply "see tasks/TASKS.md". The runner must fill test_cmd — Phase B can't edit tools/auto/queue.json (RUNNER_OWNED). Per CFG-001 plan §5: "test_cmd is for scheduler to backfill into tools/auto/queue.json; this ticket does not self-modify queue.json." Recommend test_cmd = `python3 -B tests/unit/run_fsm001_checks.py`. Runner is isolated HOME (per CFG-001, Godot may write to the user directory; use evidence-local temp HOME), no repo writes, exit code 0 only if all steps are 0 and PASS markers present, no SCRIPT ERROR.

Actually — do the headless runs of the FSM tests write anything into the repo? The `.godot/` cache is gitignored. The CORE/CFG runner used a temp HOME for editor-import step1. Same for the FSM runner: step1 editor --quit imports the new scripts. Good.

5. Also, the FSM must not touch user:// or files — pure RefCounted. Catch candidates only emit events; GameState transactions (adding to the basket, gold) are ECO-001 — the FSM must not mutate wallet/basket. Note: basket-full blocks cast — but the basket is GameState, owned by ECO-001. can_cast(game_state) → bool checks basket.size() >= capacity → false. In FSM-001 the FSM receives a read-only view of GameState (GameState is read-only — GameState lives in scripts/core, outside the allowed scope, so the FSM code can *read* it; GameState files are not modified). can_cast(game_state: GameState) → bool.

6. Settlement: at SETTLEMENT the FSM produces a catch candidate {event_id, species_id, ...}; ack_settlement(event_id, committed) → transitions to next state. Idempotency: repeated ack with the same event_id does not double-advance. event_id must be deterministic under a seed (from the RNG stream) so that the sequence is reproducible; also species selection is weighted by catch_weight/sum.

7. 20–60 s sampling from the config min/max: use runtime config's bite_wait_min_sec/max. Values must be within [min,max].

8. Pause: while paused tick_effective contributes nothing; no extra transactions; resume_if_safe. Also window-hidden semantics: OPEN-001 has been adjudicated — hidden pauses effective time; but actual window handling is the UI ticket; in FSM-001 just model pause/resume.

9. Multi-step crossing thresholds: INTERFACES §4: "if a single step crosses multiple time thresholds, it must not spuriously emit multiple catches; either define a safe at-most-one advance or explicit split scheduling" — the plan should define: tick_effective advances at most one threshold per call (e.g. one HOOKED per tick call; remaining time carries over), or split scheduling. Define: at-most-one state transition per tick_effective call, remainder retained; deterministic.

10. Risk: Godot RNG determinism — avoid it by using a custom deterministic integer PRNG; don't use RandomNumberGenerator for the production sequence? Actually RandomNumberGenerator is documented as deterministic per PCG32 given a seed but... safest for test reproducibility is to implement our own SplitMix64/xoshiro inside GDScript. Document this.

11. 30 FPS decoupling: FSM never references Engine.get_frames_drawn/_process; headless test simulates 30/15/120 FPS by calling tick_effective with different delta subdivisions summing to the same total; assert identical event log.

12. Rollback: all new untracked files under scripts/fishing/ and tests/unit/; rollback = delete those files only; git checkout not needed (no tracked file changes). Baseline HEAD 7e726f6.

13. Acceptance mapping: T-FSM-01, T-TIME-01, T-TIME-02, plus pause-related T-TIME-03 partial, V01-F01, V01-F02, V01-W03 (logic decoupling), V01-T01 (controllable clock, fixed seed, replayable sequence), SDD-143/176/177, AGENTS §4.

