Design details:

New files (all new, untracked, within scope):
- scripts/fishing/fishing_state_machine.gd — `class_name FishingStateMachine extends RefCounted`: FSM with State enum {IDLE, CASTING, WAITING, HOOKED, REELING, SETTLEMENT, PAUSED}.
- scripts/fishing/virtual_clock.gd — `class_name VirtualClock extends RefCounted`: monotonic virtual seconds; advance(seconds) rejects negative/NaN; now().
- scripts/fishing/deterministic_rng.gd — `class_name DeterministicRng extends RefCounted`: SplitMix64 → 64-bit xorshift* integer stream; next_int(), next_unit_float() via 53-bit mantissa, next_range_float(lo,hi). Pure GDScript int arithmetic — deterministic across runs/platforms/Godot versions; do NOT use Godot's RandomNumberGenerator for the business sequence (to avoid engine-version drift).
- tests/unit/test_fsm001_fsm.gd — SceneTree test, PASS marker "FSM001 FSM PASS" / "FSM001 FSM FAIL: <step>", quit 0/1.
- tests/unit/fixtures/fsm001/*.json — optional runtime-config variants for the gate tests (min_gt_max etc. already exist in cfg001's fixtures; the FSM test can reuse res://tests/unit/fixtures/cfg001/min_gt_max.json — read-only, same tests/** scope. No problem, no new fixtures needed; keep it minimal: reuse the cfg001 fixtures.)
- tests/unit/run_fsm001_checks.py — Python standard-library runner, same as CFG-001: HOME isolated in a temp under tasks/evidence/FSM-001/; steps: import, FSM test, CORE smoke regression, CFG config regression; PASS markers required, forbid SCRIPT ERROR; exit 0/1.

Interfaces (following INTERFACES §4, semantics preserved):
- initialize(catalog: Dictionary, runtime: Dictionary, rng, clock, recovered_checkpoint: Dictionary) -> {ok, error_code} — must pass through ConfigGate.can_start_economy; failure → FSM stays in IDLE, refuses to start (rejects casting).
- can_cast(state) -> bool — basket is full → false; while casting in progress/settling → false; not started → false.
- request_cast() -> {event_id} | {rejected_reason} — only from IDLE after successful start; deterministically generate catch_event_id from RNG (seeded); set wait_seconds = clamp sample within [min,max] from config.
- tick_effective(seconds) -> transitions: seconds > 0; uses VirtualClock; only WAITING advances elapsed_effective; when elapsed >= wait_seconds → HOOKED (at most 1 state transition per call, leftover carries over to the next call — INTERFACES §4 "at most 1 safe advance or explicit split scheduling"); CASTING→WAITING similarly at most 1 per call; HOOKED→REELING→SETTLEMENT require minimum phase time or explicit calls? Keep it minimal: HOOKED/REELING have configurable durations (OPEN-004: casting/reeling presentation durations are configurable and don't affect economy), elapsed also advances; SETTLEMENT → produce_catch_candidate(); ack_settlement(event_id, committed) → if committed is true → IDLE (or allow the next casting), if false → stays in SETTLEMENT, safe to retry; same event_id double-acked → AlreadyApplied with no additional transaction.
- produce_catch_candidate() -> {event_id, species_id, caught_at_clock, weight snapshot} — weighted by catch_weight/sum from the injected RNG's deterministic stream.
- pause(reason) / resume_if_safe() — while PAUSED, tick_effective contributes 0 to elapsed; no new events/transactions; resume only from PAUSED.
- snapshot_checkpoint() -> Dictionary matching GameState.fishing_checkpoint format {state, event_id, wait_seconds, elapsed_effective_seconds} + clock snapshot; initialize() with a restored checkpoint restores the same state so that continuation with the same seed reproduces the sequence.

Invariants:
- Pure RefCounted; no Node/_process/Engine.get_frames_drawn/Engine.time_scale; no user://, no file writes; do NOT modify GameState (basket/gold are ECO-001's responsibility) — FSM only emits candidates and reads state for can_cast.
- Wait times sampled from the injected deterministic RNG are always within [min,max] as configured; config values 20/60 are not to be modified; the ticket forbids parameter tuning.
- Invalid transitions (e.g. IDLE→HOOKED, WAITING→SETTLEMENT, casting from PAUSED) are rejected with a stable error code and are recorded in an in-memory transition log for testing (no file I/O — logging is LOG-001).
- Same (seed, config, clock steps, actions) ⇒ identical event sequence (test compares event logs serialized across runs).
